    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup centers on a high-upside play in **Geraldo Perdomo**, who leads our roster with a 68.61 efficiency score. Facing Zach Agnos (5.15 xERA), **Geraldo Perdomo** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill adjustment, positioning him as our most reliable engine for counting stats despite a slight penalty for platoon splits. Close behind is **Tyler Freeman** (66.93), who capitalizes on a favorable matchup against Eduardo Rodriguez. With the lineup still pending, we are banking on the assumed #3 spot for **Tyler Freeman** to maximize his RBI opportunities, as his park and skill advantages outweigh the relative neutrality of the platoon. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (66.66) remains a set-and-forget anchor; despite a tough matchup against Mize and a slight downgrade due to the opponent's ability to control the run game, his high spot in the order ensures he stays in the elite tier of our daily projections.\n\nThe most difficult decision today involved **Lawrence Butler** (58.68), who just missed the \"Strong\" threshold but remains our primary high-velocity threat. His score was bolstered by a 13% boost from platoon adjustments, making him a critical weapon in our pursuit of stolen bases, even if his spot in the lower half of the order suppresses his counting stat potential. Conversely, **Masyn Winn** (43.36) is our most marginal start, facing the stiffest test of the day against Ashcraft. The projection is hampered by a significant negative adjustment for Ashcraft\u2019s elite catcher, which suppresses **Masyn Winn**'s propensity for swiping bags. **Daulton Varsho** (55.41) occupies a similar space; while his park factor is positive, the 10% penalty for the platoon disadvantage against Carlos Rod\u00f3n makes him a high-risk, high-reward play that we are monitoring closely until official lineups drop. We continue to hold **Cal Raleigh**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Bryson Stott**, and **Will Smith** on the bench due to injuries or lack of scheduled games, leaving us with zero margin for error in our game cap management for **Taylor Ward**, **Matt Chapman**, **Luis Arraez**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Jonathan Aranda**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Gavin Sheets**, and **Drew Gilbert**.",
